WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:05.624
The check is the plan's Gate 1 test,
emergency access accounts tested,

3
00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:08.763
and the alert watches the
accounts between drills.

4
00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:13.266
It supports NIST special publication
eight hundred fifty-three A C two,

5
00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:17.083
with emergency accounts as a
defined account type, and I A two,

6
00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:21.587
enhancement one, multifactor
authentication to privileged accounts.

7
00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:27.487
The alert supports A C two,
enhancement four, A U six and S I four.

8
00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:32.632
And from CISA's B O D twenty-five
oh-one and its ScubaGear baseline:

9
00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:37.110
M S A A D seven point three,
cloud-only privileged accounts,

10
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.826
and three point six, phishing-resistant
M F A for highly privileged roles.

11
00:00:42.826 --> 00:00:47.625
Treating the drills as compensating
controls is the workbook's design guidance.

12
00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:50.001
The evidence an ISSO keeps for Gate 1:

13
00:00:50.001 --> 00:00:53.564
the findings with no finding
from the test tenant's run;

14
00:00:53.564 --> 00:00:56.099
the drill tickets and the drill record;

15
00:00:56.099 --> 00:01:00.910
the reviewed alert template and its
deployment record; and the manifest.
